   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello, I have been trying to create a SPDE model for some snow data, the problem I am running across is that when i make my mesh for all the locations that the snow is being sampled at there are dates that are missing from locations, for example if i had a sample for every date at each location id have 25,000 observations but I have a bit over 17,000. Is there a way to make a model that can go across all time and use all the data i have. Anybody know how to handle this?<div><br></div><div>Thanks</div><div>Clinton Woods<br><div><br></div><div>Some basic code:<br><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">c </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cbind</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xy$lon</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xy$lat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></font><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>bound </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> inla</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nonconvex</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hull</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">points </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                             convex </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                             concave </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>mesh </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> inla</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mesh</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2d</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> boundary </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> bound</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                     max</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">edge </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                     cutoff </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>spde </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> inla</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">spde2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">matern</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mesh </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mesh</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># hard to make an indicator because each measurement site might have different numbers of observations threw time. </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>SS$time </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(?,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> each </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">115</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>A </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> inla</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">spde</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">make</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">A</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mesh </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mesh</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                      loc </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> SS$Y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                      n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">287</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
